  "description": "It was discovered that FontForge incorrectly handled memory when reading\nSFD files, leading to a use-after-free. If a user or automated system were\ntricked into opening a specially crafted SFD file, an attacker could\npossibly use this issue to cause FontForge to crash, resulting in a denial\nof service, or possibly execute arbitrary code. (CVE-2020-5395)\n\nIt was discovered that FontForge incorrectly handled certain SFD files,\nleading to a heap-based buffer overflow. If a user or automated system were\ntricked into opening a specially crafted SFD file, an attacker could\npossibly use this issue to cause FontForge to crash, resulting in a denial\nof service, or possibly execute arbitrary code. (CVE-2020-5496)",
  "id": "USN-9138-1",
  "isummary": "FontForge could be made to crash or run programs as your login if it opened\na specially crafted file.",
